def power-input-jst
  title "5 V input: JST PH connector, reverse-polarity diode, capacitor"
  about "Two-wire supply input as in the edakit example: JST PH 2-pin connector, SS34 Schottky diode against reverse
      polarity (drops 0.3–0.5 V), 22 µF behind it."
  port out "the protected supply rail"
  port gnd "ground"
  part J1 connector B2B-PH-K-S(LF)(SN) lcsc C131337 "{as}: supply input (JST PH, pin 1 = +)"
    notes "Pin 1 = +, pin 2 = GND."
  part D1 diode SS34 lcsc C8678 "{as}: reverse-polarity protection"
  part C1 capacitor CL21A226MAQNNNE lcsc C45783 value 22uF "{as}: 22 µF at the input"
    notes "X5R: at 5 V only about 30–50 % of the 22 µF are left (DC bias)."
  net vin 0..5.5 V J1.1 D1.anode
    notes "Connector side of the diode; for another supply voltage change v here and on the output."
  net out 0..5.5 V D1.cathode C1.1
  net gnd J1.2 C1.2
  covers PATH.reverse HINT.bulk
  notes "Graph: give the connector \"source\": \"reversible\" – PATH.reverse then checks that a reversed plug reaches
      only the diode's anode."
  notes "sim.json: the connector under sources (plus \"1\", minus \"2\") and its voltages under supplies."
  notes "The 22 µF ceramic is the buffer of the example; for long cables or plugging in while powered add an
      electrolytic (hint HINT.bulk)."
